  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district; governmental funds only (General incl. Depreciation, plus School Nutrition, Special Building, Activities). Statement p4-6 Total Governmental Funds column. Roll: 6,032,081 + 6,128,215 - 5,253,625 + 146,000 - 146,000 = 6,906,671. Cash basis so beginning/ending cash = fund balance (all assets are cash/CDs/county treasurer cash). Transfer cross-check: General Fund transfer out 146,000 (p9, inside its schedule total 4,880,746, shown as separate line, excluded from statement disbursements) = School Nutrition 46,000 + Activities 100,000 transfers in (p10); recorded as other financing, not spending. Balance sheet from the government-wide net position section (p3); no liabilities printed. Detail is from the budget-and-actual schedules pp12-18 (General pp12-14 with federal receipts by program, Depreciation p15, School Nutrition p16 by object, Special Building p17, Activities p18), with budget_final; they replace the combining-schedule lines (pp8-10) to avoid double counting. Depreciation capital outlay and Special Building capital improvements were budgeted (523,527; 390,809) but had no actual spending (recorded as 0). Code 2110 County fines and license fees 22,163 (statement label 'County and ESU sources') is fines and forfeitures per the school code rule. Special Building Fund has no disbursements. Read pages 1-18 of 18"
